web/node_modules/jsdom/README.md:If you are simply trying to execute script "from the outside", instead of letting `<script>` elements and event handlers attributes run "from the inside", you can use the `runScripts: "outside-only"` option, which enables fresh copies of all the JavaScript spec-provided globals to be installed on `window`. This includes things like `window.Array`, `window.Promise`, etc. It also, notably, includes `window.eval`, which allows running scripts, but with the jsdom `window` as the global:
